# 75. FINAL DESIGN DIRECTION

So the reference image gives us the **visual DNA**:

> **Dark premium hero + editorial typography + large photography + whitespace + orange CTA + elegant cards + dark footer.**

The Nest poster gives us the **brand DNA**:

> **NEST LIBRARY + bird/nest logo + navy/orange/gold + Self Study Center + Co-working Space + Better Space Bigger Dreams.**

The Prime website work gives us the **business UX DNA**:

> **strong CTA + WhatsApp + booking + enquiry + offer popup + responsive design + conversion tracking + local SEO + business-ready architecture.**

And the library research gives us the **product DNA**:

> **study-space discovery + facilities + seat information + policies + availability architecture + memberships + future reservations + attendance + renewals.**

Put those four together and **that is the Nest UI direction I would give the frontend agent**.

